    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py`. I didn't run or test it, as instructed.\n\n- **Validation:** it raises `TypeError` if `start` isn't a plain `date` (a `datetime` is rejected), if `n` isn't an `int` (`bool` and `float` are rejected), or if any holiday isn't a plain `date`. Holidays are collected into a set first, so generators work and bad elements are caught up front.\n- **`n > 0` or `n < 0`:** it steps one day at a time in that direction from `start`. It counts only Monday–Friday dates that aren't holidays, until it has counted `|n|` of them. `start` itself is never counted.\n- **`n == 0`:** it returns `start` if it's a business day, otherwise the next business day after it.\n\nHolidays that fall on a weekend change nothing.",
